{
 "gdd": "design/gdd/derelict-authoring-handmade-kits.md",
 "blockers": [
  {
   "where": "L324, L739, L1886, L1888 (amended hunks, ADR-0012 sync) against L332, L1046 (D.14 row), L1997 (AC-DA-75)",
   "issue": "The amended text says the persisted `isolated_at_step` stamp is 'the form of the `intensity_pm` > 0 test', so the two gates are equivalent. They are not. ADR-0012 § 8.4 and LS-11 stamp `isolated_at` only when a closed VALVE drives the descriptor to 0. `pb_leak` is a LEAK at `hp` 2900 with intensity 0 because B is dry and cold (a SCRAMmed `r_b`, no flow), not because of a valve, and V12 is the reactor hand crank. Under the new gate its stamp is 0, so it wears from step 0. L332 and L1046 still say 'held at 2900 while dry; 91 periods counted from V12'. AC-DA-75 still asserts `hp` constant for `pb_leak` before V12. The D.21 and V12 race arithmetic (hp 2900 at V12, 6 mL per step, margin 8,500 mL) also assumes no wear before V12. An implementer who follows the amended gate will find the pb_leak clock, the AC and the race table fail.",
   "fix": "Pick one and state it. (a) Add an isolating closed valve upstream of `pb_leak`, which changes layout, so it needs the level-designer. (b) Seed a non-zero `isolated_at_step` in the pb_leak M1 row, which ADR-0012 § 8.4 allows through the seeded triple, and say that V12 or the first flow clears it. (c) Raise it with the Graph owner and ADR-0012 to define 'dry' as isolated for wear. Then re-word the 'equivalent form' claim as 'equivalent only behind a closed valve', and restrict the AC-DA-75 'intensity_pm 0 means hp constant' clause to `d_cryo_exposed` (valve) and `pa_frozen` (forced FREEZE)."
  },
  {
   "where": "AC-DA-97 (L2044)",
   "issue": "The clause 'changing one authored value by 1 (`b_main` `stock` by 1 dJ) changes the template hashes (`geometry_hash`, `visual_hash`, `structure_hash`, as the edit touches them) and `state_hash`' cannot be tested. ADR-0013 § 3 defines the three hashes over geometry, presentation and ordered keys only. None of them covers a Graph node's initial `stock`, `hp` or `breaker_closed`, so this edit touches none of the three. 'As the edit touches them' lets the assertion pass vacuously or fail depending on how it is read. The old single `template_hash` hid this.",
   "fix": "Split the clause. A stock, `hp`, charge or switch edit changes `state_hash` and leaves all three Layout hashes unchanged. A wall, door or socket move changes `geometry_hash`. A kit-piece or label change changes `visual_hash`. A reorder, rename, add or remove of a key changes `structure_hash`. Align DA-35 ('a template edit changes `state_hash`') to the same split."
  }
 ]
}
